# generic_instance_from_use - a generic enum's variant or a generic class's construction is the instance its use names: a variant argument takes the instance its parameter has once the call's type arguments are bound (`first_ok(Result::Ok(4), 9)` for `r: Result<T, T>`), type arguments written on a variant call name it (`Result::Ok::<i32, i32>(4)`), and a generic class constructed by value is the instance its type arguments or its expected type name (`Cell::<i32>(4)`, `const c: Cell<i32> = Cell(4);`).
